From 987a9c1bb3a7a014885aace66d37412f6b6d6832 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lane <lane@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 04:36:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] generator: extend runtime-define contract to 4 more programs;
 find + exclude halftone

Four more define-backed parameters move from default-only to the generic
runtime-int contract (tools/glslcpp/generate_typed_slice.py's
GENERIC_DYNAMIC_DEFINE_TYPES): filter/oilPaint:oilFlatten+oilPost (MODE),
filter/strokes:stkPost (MODE, unreferenced by this pass's own source -- a
pure bookkeeping uniform), filter/stipple:stipple (MODE), and
filter/pondRipples:pondRipples (STYLE, WRAP). Each validates and lowers
cleanly under the existing frontend (preprocess.py's runtime-if lowering,
dynamic_define_hoist.py) with no new capability or construct -- oilPost and
stkPost needed nothing beyond the table entry; oilFlatten needed a relock of
its existing ceil_admission_profile (the int(ceil(fr)) site is unconditional
on MODE, only its node ids shifted); stipple and pondRipples needed a relock
of the existing multi-key derivative_admission_profile (their fwidth/dFdx/
dFdy call sites are likewise unconditional on the promoted defines).

filter/halftone:halftone (MODE, PATTERN) was promoted, relocked, and then
REVERTED after tools/parity/sweep.py's ordinary (non-define-enum) sweep --
which draws random ink/paper hex colors, unlike the define-enum mode's
default-held-elsewhere isolation -- found a real divergence at MODE=1
(mono): the JS authority's tonemap2(t, inkColor, paperColor) mix leaks the
hex color's alpha nibble into the rendered alpha channel, even though the
GLSL declares inkColor/paperColor as vec3. The C++ port correctly narrows
to Vec3 at bind time and threads the separately-sampled input alpha instead,
so every MODE=1 pixel comes out fully opaque (255) against the authority's
actual (translucent) alpha. MODE=0 (color/CMYK) never calls tonemap2 and is
unaffected -- confirmed by an isolated ordinary sweep against the pre-change
baseline binary, which only ever draws MODE=0 (every non-default MODE
request is refused there) and shows zero divergence. GENERIC_DYNAMIC_DEFINE_TYPES
promotes a whole program, not one value, so halftone stays default-only
until the vec4-vs-vec3 ink/paper materialization contract is modeled --
same posture this lane inherited for filter/scatter's excluded MODE=3.

filter/strokes:stkSmear (also MODE) is untouched and still default-only:
its MODE lives inside a called function (srcSample), gated by a forward
declaration, and needs its own scoped proof. Because "mode" is one catalog
parameter bound to both strokes passes, the whole effect still correctly
reports cpp_refused_only for non-default MODE.

Regenerated via regen_all.sh to REGEN OK. Native suite: 586 pass, 1 fail
(typed_classic_noise_oracle_metadata_is_complete_and_load_bearing, owned
elsewhere per the task brief). tests.test_dsl_corpus_parity: pass.
test_semantic.py: 33/33. test_typed_generator.py: fixed three real
regressions this landing caused (Task33DerivativeAdmissionTests.exact_program
now builds the dynamic tree for stipple/pondRipples, matching what
generate_outputs() actually emits; test_committed_manifest_...'s and
test_task25_...'s frozen define_contract/whole-file-hash pins updated to the
new correct values) and left ~19 other failing methods (~48 assertions)
alone after reproducing every one of them identically against a pristine
06d77bd archive -- confirmed pre-existing, unrelated to this change.

Sweep evidence (NOISEMAKER_DSL_CPU_CASE built from this tree):
- --define-enum --effects oilPaint,strokes,stipple,pondRipples: 156
  byte_exact, 0 divergent, 0 both_refused, 0 timeout, 24 cpp_refused_only
  (all filter/strokes, the untouched stkSmear pass).
- ordinary --variants 20, same effects: 75 byte_exact + 10/12 chains
  byte_exact, 0 divergent, 0 timeout, 17+2 cpp_refused_only (same strokes
  cause).
- Full-corpus regression, --variants 6, before (06d77bd baseline binary)
  vs after (this tree), 1423/1423 matched case_ids: 15 cpp_refused_only ->
  byte_exact (exactly the 4 landed programs' cases), 0 -> divergent, 0
  genuine regressions. 31 cases flipped cpp_refused_only -> timeout, all
  unrelated 3D programs (render3d family, synth3d/*) never touched here;
  an isolated single-worker, 180s-budget re-run of one of them
  (render/render3d) reproduces the baseline's cpp_refused_only exactly,
  confirming shared-machine CPU contention (other concurrent lanes) as the
  cause, not a code regression.

